owards the back entrance of the  firefort tavern which opens onto a white  cold street on a slight incline fog can  be seen all around obscuring the rest of  the street the sounds of revelry coming  from inside the firefall can be heard a  man in his thirties wearing a long thick  great coat is smoking a cigarillo  outside the entrance ramirez approaches  him  hello  juan lumiere  the very same you're that foundation  girl  aren't you  staying at the dragoman  junior researcher sophia ramirez  a lovely name  i can only presume given that recording  device on your shoulder that you'll come  to interview me  if we could step inside i prefer to  stand down here  they are bright and merry in there  i'll wait until the fire is lower and  the company more selective  let the young have their fun how old are  you  278  but don't look it do i  the perks of this city i've aged six  years in the time i've been here by my  county  but nobody ever comes here for eternal  life  i've been wondering about that  it's because it doesn't feel like it's  meant to  you don't feel like you're living longer  just that those years have been spread  out longer like skin stretched over a  drum you never develop properly  your writing has  i didn't think anyone in saul had ever  heard of me  it  well if i'm honest it was your work that  first drew me here  you're unusual  your later stuff talks about fire and  light but with much more craft than most  of the other long-termers  you were like the newer ones then i  i do quite like them  but you're like the earlier ones more  everyone likes the earlier ones more  they just don't understand why someone  would come to lamplight just to write  about the things in their own lives to  them in their private salons this place  is just the wild frontier  the mystery beyond mysteries the edge of  all creation they want something wild  not something homespun  isn't that natural  do you write at all  compose  i  i play a little violin  i write some of the